iculum\nClinical Rotations\nSupplementary Activities\nPeople\nAlways Here to Help\nAdministrative Staff\nOrganizational Structure and Committees\nFaculty Directory\nFaculty\nGenetic Counselling Faculty\nPostdocs\nAlumni\nAbout\nAbout Us\nChair's Message\nHistory\nResearch Locations\nOutreach in Molecular Genetics\nNews\nNewsletters\nEvents\nSeminars\nUpcoming Info Sessions\nLinks and Resources\nEquity, Diversity, & Inclusion in MoGen\nPositions\nMain Second Level Navigation\nGraduate Admissions\nAcademic Requirements\nApplication Procedures\nDeadlines\nFAQs\nInternational Students\nResearch Areas\nAlways Here to Help\nCurriculum\nGraduate Resources\nStudent Supervision\nTeaching Assistantships\nAfter Graduation\nBack to Admissions Page\nBreadcrumbs\nHome\nMolecular Genetics MSc/PhD\nGraduate Admissions\nDeadlines\nDeadlines\nWhen to submit application and supporting documents\nDeadlines have changed from previous years\nPlease review deadline information carefully, as dates have changed from previous application cycles.\nApplications for this year's admissions cycle will be accepted starting on October 5, 2026, for Fall 2027 (September) start.\nApplications from domestic students (Canadian citizens and permanent residents) will be accepted until January 15, 2027. Depending on the volume of applications and availability of remaining spots, applications from domestic applicants may still be accepted on a rolling basis after January 15; however, this is not guaranteed. Please check back on this page for the status of rolling admissions.\nApplications from international students (those requiring study permits) will be accepted until November 15, 2026, to account for timelines for study permit processing and international awards. International applications that are not complete by this deadline will not be reviewed. International applicants should review the international students page for important information about additional requirements. An application will not be considered complete without all required components.\nStudents who are currently completing an MSc in our department and interested in returning for a PhD with us should contact the department's Learning Strategist to discuss, as there are key procedures and alternate timelines to be aware of.\nApplication And Document Submission Deadlines\nPlease ensure that all supporting documents (references, electronic transcripts, CV and letter of intent) are submitted online by the respective deadline. It's also important to verify that materials are uploaded under the correct checklist item; if a checklist item is missing a document or has an incorrect document uploaded, the application will not be considered complete.\nIt is entirely the applicant's responsibility to monitor the status of their documents on the online application system and follow up with their referees if references are not received in advance of the deadline. Only complete applications will be reviewed for admission.\nYour application will be reviewed and a decision will be made within a couple of months from the deadline.\nNote that the Department of Molecular Genetics does not have fixed enrollment quotas; the size of the incoming cohort is dependent on both the availability of lab positions and the strength of applications under consideration.\nAccepting Our Offer\nStudents who receive an offer of admission should confirm their reply to our offer as soon as possible. We request that applicants return their confirmation forms, indicating their intention, by the date stated on the offer letter. We will consider requests for deferred admission.\nEntrance Scholarships\nConnaught International Scholarship.\nC. David Naylor University Fellowships\nSGS Admissions Awards\nDepartment of Molecular Genetics\nUniversity of Toronto\nRoom 4203, Medical Sciences Building\n1 King's College Circle\nToronto, ON M5S 1A8\nCanada\nFollow us on Facebook\nFollow us on LinkedIn\nFollow us on Twitter\nFollow us on Instagram\nFol